  "facts": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "West Hillhurst was annexed by Calgary in 1907 but saw major growth only after WWII when Victory Homes were built for returning soldiers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Hillhurst%2C_Calgary"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The neighborhood’s first paved roads appeared in 1910 and a streetcar line arrived in 1913, linking it to downtown early on.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.heritageinspiresyyc.org/heritage-places/communities-west-hillhurst/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A 1960s bridge over the Bow River and the creation of Crowchild Trail split West Hillhurst, a change still visible in its layout today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16,
        17,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.heritageinspiresyyc.org/heritage-places/communities-west-hillhurst/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "West Hillhurst’s roots trace back to the Riley farm, owned by a prominent pioneer family, and the area once bore names like Westmount and Grand Trunk.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.heritageinspiresyyc.org/heritage-places/communities-west-hillhurst/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The community center, outdoor rinks, churches, and retail shops make West Hillhurst a stable, low‑density enclave of single‑family homes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.heritageinspiresyyc.org/heritage-places/communities-west-hillhurst/"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Despite being built as temporary Victory Homes, many of those houses remain standing, giving the neighborhood a unique wartime architectural legacy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
